Package: tidyagsim
Title: Tidymodels-Style Tuning and Replication for 'AlphaSimR' and Other Breeding Simulations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jay", "Gillenwater", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "55106933+jhgille2@users.noreply.github.com"))
Description: Extends 'AlphaSimR' with the grammar of the 'tidymodels'
    packages, so that plant breeding simulation studies are set up like a
    model-tuning job. Write a breeding scheme once, mark its design choices
    with tune(), describe replicate seeds and assumption scenarios, choose a
    metric set, and let grid search, racing or Bayesian optimization run the
    experiment without enumerating every combination by hand. Results are tidy
    tibbles with Monte Carlo standard errors, and helpers such as show_best(),
    select_by_one_std_err() and pareto_front() pick designs. Includes a
    ready-made inbred line pipeline, a fast simulator for QTL mapping
    populations (F2, recombinant inbred lines, BCsFt, nested association
    mapping, advanced-backcross NAM and MAGIC), and engines for any R function
    and for 'breedsim' breeding-program flowcharts.
